        "font" : "CMR10",
        "font size" : 9.963,
        "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
        "content" : "In that case, the boundary of each face in G is a cycle. Assume that c is the smallest number of vertices that need to be removed from G to make it Ck-free, and let v1,v2,...,vc be one such set of vertices. Then c ≤ k, since we can remove vertices of a k-cycle to make it Ck-free. Moreover, for any i,j ∈ [c], there exists a k-cycle in G such that vi is contained in the k-cycle, but vj not."
      } ]
