    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Since G is 2-connected, it follows that G′ = G − v1 is connected and is Ck-free. Assume that G′ has r blocks B1,B2,...,Br, where |Bi| ≥ klog2 3 for i ∈ [q] and |Bi| < klog2 3 for q + 1 ≤ i ≤ r. For each i ∈ [q], since Bi is a Ck-free 2-connected plane graph, it follows that"
